# ask-this-book

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root: repo map, the guarantees the tests hold, run
and verify commands, operational facts. Then `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for the
pipeline and `docs/OPERATIONS.md` for install/measure/troubleshoot.
`GLOSSARY.md` translates the vocabulary when a term is unclear.

`GOAL.md` and `BUILD_PLAN.md` were removed on 2026-11-01 — they were stale and
confused agents. Do not recreate a goal or plan document; put a decision in the
code, a test, or a dated file under `artifacts/`.

## Artifacts

- Never write an artifact to the repo root or to a new flat path under
  `artifacts/`; only `prune.py` and `README.md` sit at its top level.
- Consult the decision list in `artifacts/README.md` before creating anything.
- Every artifact carries its date: `family-YYYY-MM-DD[-label].ext`.
- A run is promoted into `artifacts/` only when a doc or commit names it;
  otherwise it stays in `artifacts/runs/` or `artifacts/scratch/`.
